# Normalize line endings to LF in the working tree, not just in the repository.
#
# Why this exists: Prettier's `endOfLine` default is "lf", and this repo's
# `npm run format` (`prettier --check .`) is the first step of `npm run verify`.
# On Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites files to CRLF on checkout, which
# makes those files fail `prettier --check` even when their committed content
# is byte-for-byte correct. That produced a real, confusing failure: two files
# started failing `verify` immediately after a plain `git checkout --` of them,
# with an empty `git diff` and identical blob hashes.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf` for this repository, so checkouts match
# what Prettier and CI expect on every platform. Binary files are excluded
# below so git never applies text filtering to them.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never line-ending-filtered, never diffed as text.
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.webm binary
*.mp3 binary
*.wav binary
